<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n116047" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὠγῠγία</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>Ogygia,</i> a mythical island in
			the Mediterranean, the abode of Calypso, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				1.85
			</span></i> (written <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὠγυλίη</span></b> 
			by <i><span class="en">
				Antim.
			</span></i>, Sch. l.c.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			epith.(?) of <i>Egypt,</i> Eust.ad <i><span class="en">
				D.P.
				239
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> of
				<u>Attica</u> and <i>Boeotia,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				St.Byz.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b> an island west of
			Britain in which Kronos was imprisoned, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.941a
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
